1.05

  Summary: additive patch, idle PDA reworked, companion and patrol freeze fixed, wounded stand-up, poses restored, wall-facing fix, performance, MCM config

  First release of this fork of Chemzs's xAGNA. Every entry below is a change against that original.

  Compatibility
    - Every script in the mod was remade from the ground up. The data, the animation and state tables, now sits apart from the code, and the code adds its changes at load,
      wrapping or replacing a vanilla function only where that fits. The original instead shipped whole copies of the game's core animation and state scripts, which overwrote the shared state machine.
      Any mod that also touched it lost, and companions and patrols could freeze. The additive remake should clear several of the reported bugs and odd behavior. The OMFs ship as assets, as before.
    - The relaxed standing idle uses the vanilla pose, not the varied one the original set.

  Behavior
    - Idle PDA reworked. The original drew it on the shared idle. Every NPC pulled one out, and the multi-step draw froze them in place. That blocked patrol and companions. The idle is instant again.
      Now only standing, calm, out-of-combat NPCs near you occasionally take one out. Never a zombie or a companion, and dropped the moment danger appears.
      It no longer takes one out of an NPC in a scripted animation, a smart cover, a patrol, or a story role.
    - Wounded NPCs play a stand-up animation as they recover, instead of snapping upright.
    - The greeting and PDA an NPC plays when you walk up to a commander no longer fire on every approach. Each rolls its own chance, so most approaches are a plain greeting.
    - Every chance is a slider, and a slider at 0 turns that behavior off. A wounded stand-up toggle sits alongside them.

  Vanilla fixes
    - An NPC left standing and facing a wall turns to the open side instead of staring at it. Only plain standing wall poses near you are turned. Seated, leaning, counter,
      and campfire poses are untouched. The toggle for it lives here.

  Logging
    - Added a Log level control and an immediate-flush toggle for live tracing.
    - Added an Animation sampling toggle that records the states NPCs actually play to xagna_animations.log, for confirming the mod's motions fire.

  Performance
    - Reduced the cost of the idle-PDA check. A distant NPC is rejected first, the eligibility check runs less often, and a drawn NPC is re-checked on a short interval, so a crowded area costs less.

  Animations restored
    - Sentry and listening NPCs play a tuned set per weapon slot: a look-around or listening pose on most slots, a plain idle on the rest, and a slot that borrowed another's idle now plays its own.
    - Searching NPCs play their poses on every weapon slot again.
    - NPCs searching for a bloodsucker play the alert pose again.
    - The unarmed idle cycles its 4 variants again.
    - Heavy-wounded variant 3 keeps its own distinct pose again.
    - Standing smoke plays the smoking animation again.

  Install
    - Delete the previous xAGNA before installing. It no longer ships the old override script files. Leaving them in place re-applies the old behavior.
